cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its certificates, please cite it as below."
title: "Exactly Verifiable Infeasibility Certificates for Robot Motion Planning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cambon
    given-names: Stéphane
    affiliation: Cambon AI
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/stephanecambon/no-plan"
abstract: >-
  Infeasibility certificates for motion planning of articulated arms that an
  independent 499-line standard-library verifier re-checks in exact rational
  arithmetic. The method combines a rational parametrization of forward
  kinematics, a low-degree barrier whose slab separates start from goal inside
  the obstacle region, and per-cell witnesses found by linear programming over
  Bernstein coefficients. Includes the verifier, the generator, the scene files,
  the certificates of every certified scene (up to a 7-DOF KUKA iiwa7), and the
  dated benchmark files the paper reads its numbers from.
keywords:
  - motion planning
  - infeasibility certificate
  - path non-existence
  - exact arithmetic
  - Bernstein polynomials
  - linear programming
  - configuration space
  - robot manipulators
